<title>USA: Duff &amp; Phelps assigns BB rating to Argentina bonds.</title>
<headline>Duff &amp; Phelps assigns BB rating to Argentina bonds.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said in a release received here that it assigned a Double B rating to the one billion Deutsche mark bonds offered Tuesday by the Republic of Argentina.</p>
<p>The bonds have a coupon of 8.5 percent and mature February 23, 2005.</p>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps said its rating for Argentina's long-term foreign currency obligations reflects the country's proven commitment to economic reforms.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
</text>
